📱 COMPLETE TECH STACK GUIDE FOR CURSOR AI
🎯 PROJECT: Belebi Prayer - React Native Mobile App
TECH STACK OVERVIEW
This is a React Native mobile app built with the following stack:

Core Technologies:
✅ Expo SDK - Managed React Native framework
✅ Expo Dev Client - Custom development build (NOT Expo Go)
✅ NativeWind v4 - Tailwind CSS for React Native
✅ React Navigation - Navigation library
✅ TypeScript - Type safety
✅ Lucide React Native - Icon library
WHY THIS STACK?
1. Expo + Expo Dev Client (NOT Expo Go)
Expo Go = Limited, can't use custom native modules
Expo Dev Client = Full power of React Native + Expo's developer experience
Allows use of ANY native library while keeping Expo's benefits
Fast Refresh, OTA updates, easy builds
2. NativeWind v4
Tailwind CSS syntax for React Native
Write className just like web (converts to StyleSheet automatically)
Preserves all your existing color palette and design system
Syntax: className="bg-[#fdfcfb] p-4 rounded-xl"
3. React Navigation
Industry standard for RN navigation
Stack, Drawer, and Tab navigators
Deep linking support
INSTALLATION COMMANDS
Step 1: Create Expo Project
npx create-expo-app@latest belebi-prayer-mobile --template blank-typescript
cd belebi-prayer-mobile
Step 2: Install Expo Dev Client
npx expo install expo-dev-client
Step 3: Install NativeWind v4
npm install nativewind
npm install --save-dev tailwindcss@3.3.2
Step 4: Install Navigation
npx expo install @react-navigation/native @react-navigation/native-stack @react-navigation/drawer
npx expo install react-native-screens react-native-safe-area-context react-native-gesture-handler react-native-reanimated
Step 5: Install UI Dependencies
npx expo install expo-linear-gradient
npx expo install @react-native-picker/picker
npx expo install lucide-react-native
