KEY CODE PATTERNS
1. Screens Use React Native Components
import { View, Text, ScrollView, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

// NOT web <div>, <p>, <button>
// USE: <View>, <Text>, <TouchableOpacity>
2. Navigation
import { useNavigation } from '@react-navigation/native';
import { NativeStackNavigationProp } from '@react-navigation/native-stack';

type NavigationProp = NativeStackNavigationProp<RootStackParamList>;
const navigation = useNavigation<NavigationProp>();

// Navigate
navigation.navigate('ScreenName', { params });

// Go back
navigation.goBack();
3. Styling - Two Approaches
Option A: StyleSheet (Recommended)

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    backgroundColor: '#fdfcfb',
    padding: 16,
  },
});

<View style={styles.container}>...</View>
Option B: NativeWind (Tailwind-like)

<View className="flex-1 bg-[#fdfcfb] p-4">...</View>
4. Icons - Lucide React Native
import { Heart, Globe, Send } from 'lucide-react-native';

<Heart size={24} color="#6B4F3E" />
5. No CSS Files in Screens
NO import './styles.css'
Use StyleSheet.create() or NativeWind className
RUNNING THE APP
Development Build (First Time)
# iOS
npx expo run:ios

# Android
npx expo run:android
After First Build (Fast Refresh)
npx expo start --dev-client
Build for Production
# iOS
eas build --platform ios

# Android
eas build --platform android
CRITICAL DIFFERENCES FROM WEB
Web React	React Native
<div>	<View>
<p>, <span>, <h1>	<Text>
<button>	<TouchableOpacity> or <Pressable>
<input>	<TextInput>
<img>	<Image>
onClick	onPress
onChange	onChangeText (for TextInput)
CSS files	StyleSheet.create()
className	style prop (or NativeWind className)
style={{ }} (camelCase)	style={{ }} (same)
<select>	<Picker> from @react-native-picker/picker
window.location	React Navigation
localStorage	AsyncStorage
